1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,300
I used to think Earth would always be there.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,900
Then the cities went dark, and the sky followed.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:11,500
They called us the lucky ones. Six seats on a ship meant for hundreds.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,500
I still remember the faces we left behind.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,400
We watched our world become a tiny blue light.

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,600
Nobody spoke. There was nothing left to say.

7
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,600
The reactor failed before we reached Mars.

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,800
Our return fuel was gone.

9
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,400
Then the last transmission from Earth disappeared.

10
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:38,100
I remembered Jezero Crater from the old rover maps.

11
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,300
An ancient lake, a dried river delta.

12
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:44,500
We aimed our wounded ship toward the crater floor.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,300
Six of us survived. The air is running out.

14
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,800
The water is counted by the drop.

15
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,500
No rescue is coming.

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:59,899
If this is our last sunrise... we will build another.
